tered order, followed by descriptive degree rankings at each penalty and selection using the fixed rule?",\n    "Was degree 1 with alpha 0.0 frozen as the final configuration for this run, or is the report explicitly an intermediate document awaiting completion?",\n    "What are the host\'s exact preprocessing, polynomial feature construction, intercept treatment, penalty normalization, solver, and software version?",\n    "What does independent verification check, and can the relevant execution receipt and registered specification be included?",\n    "What evidence, beyond the existence of a numerical score, supports describing the baseline as consistent with performing well? Could this wording be restricted to documenting the hypothesized candidate\'s observed score?"\n  ],\n  "Limitations": [\n    "The report adequately acknowledges the missing comparisons, fixed-split scope, selection bias, unavailable uncertainty estimates, and absence of test measurements.",\n    "The incomplete experiment is a limitation of the available evidence rather than evidence against any unevaluated configuration. Resolving it requires completing the authorized preregistered evaluations or documenting the binding execution restriction.",\n    "A selected configuration and its validation ranking would remain conditional on this dataset, split, candidate set, and host implementation even after completion.",\n    "No concrete negative societal impact is apparent from the supplied regression task. The primary reporting risk is that a provisional singleton selection could be mistaken for validated comparative superiority; a clear completion status and final candidate table would reduce that risk."\n  ],\n  "Ethical Concerns": false,\n  "Soundness": 2,\n  "Presentation": 2,\n  "Contribution": 1,\n  "Overall": 3,\n  "Confidence": 4,\n  "Decision": "Reject"\n}\n```', True), 
